  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/SES2iVZmAuOyfB9z77qA77SZx-xh77PPMKzRKnntIHg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nMagnetic field at $P, B=\\frac{\\mu_0}{4 \\pi} \\frac{m(2 l)}{r^3}$, where $m$ is the pole strength\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\Rightarrow\\left(\\frac{\\Delta B}{B} \\times 100\\right) & =\\left(\\frac{\\Delta l}{l}\\right) \\times 100+3\\left|\\frac{\\Delta r}{r}\\right| \\times 100 \\\\\n& =1 \\%+3 \\%=4 \\%\n\\end{aligned}$",
